course: dictionary
lesson: 12644
title: Feeling down in a story
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how a character feels, and writers choose them to make you feel it too. Dispirited means having lost hope and energy, so you feel down and want to stop trying. «After the fifth loss, the team were dispirited and sat quietly on the bench.» They have lost hope, so they look gloomy.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Lost, sat quietly and no cheering all point to a sad, tired feeling. Dispirited can also describe a voice or a way of moving: «He gave a dispirited shrug when his kite snapped.» The shrug shows the feeling.
explain: Dispirited is the opposite of cheerful, encouraged and in high spirits. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The team were sad and had lost hope» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Dispirited means having lost hope and energy, and feeling down.
fact: «Dispirited» can describe a person, a voice, or a whole team.
fact: In stories, «dispirited» often comes just before help or a new idea arrives.
fact: Opposites of «dispirited» are «cheerful», «encouraged» and «in high spirits».
fact: The verb «dispirit» means to take away someone's hope or energy, as in «The rain dispirited the campers.»
exercise: «The team were dispirited after losing every game.» What does dispirited mean? | Full of energy and ready to play | *Feeling down and without hope | Very noisy and excited | Cold and wet
exercise: «Her dispirited voice showed she had almost given up.» What does the voice show? | Happiness | Surprise | *Sadness and loss of hope | Anger at the referee
exercise: Which word is the opposite of dispirited? | Gloomy | Tired | Sad | *Encouraged
test: Mia felt dispirited when her boat sank, and she sat on the sand without trying again. What does dispirited suggest? | Excited and ready to swim | She was very hungry | She was lost in a forest | *She had lost hope and energy
test: Which sentence uses dispirited correctly? | *The dispirited puppy lay by the door, too sad to play | The dispirited sun shone brightly over the park | Dispirited is a type of cake | The dispirited puppy wagged its tail and jumped up with joy
exam: Dad called, «Keep going, you can do it!», and the dispirited runner smiled again. What change does this show? | The runner was dispirited the whole race | The runner lost all hope and gave up | *The runner began to feel hopeful again | The runner had never felt sad
